WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.768
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:06.068 --> 00:00:09.257
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:17.422
Unit thirty: Wishes, Regrets and Preferences (advanced). Today you will express preferences and impatience with advanced structures.

4
00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:20.270
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:24.722
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:26.573
I'd sooner.

7
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:30.895
I'd sooner means I would prefer, in a slightly formal tone.

8
00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:33.297
I'd sooner walk than drive.

9
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:36.373
Your turn. Say: I'd sooner.

10
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:40.560
I'd sooner.

11
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:42.434
It's about time.

12
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.634
It's about time means expressing impatience for a change.

13
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.878
It's about time we left.

14
00:00:49.483 --> 00:00:52.530
Your turn. Say: It's about time.

15
00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:56.542
It's about time.

16
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:58.284
If only.

17
00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:01.805
If only means a strong wish or regret.

18
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:03.743
If only I knew.

19
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.851
Your turn. Say: If only.

20
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.689
If only.

21
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.358
Would rather.

22
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.617
Would rather means a way to state preference.

23
00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:17.798
I would rather stay home.

24
00:01:18.383 --> 00:01:20.769
Your turn. Say: Would rather.

25
00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:24.646
Would rather.

26
00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:26.326
Supposing.

27
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:29.200
Supposing means imagine that.

28
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:31.665
Supposing it rains, what then?

29
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.670
Your turn. Say: Supposing.

30
00:01:37.533 --> 00:01:38.511
Supposing.

31
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.193
Suppose.

32
00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:43.752
Suppose means to imagine as a possibility.

33
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.537
Suppose you won.

34
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.802
Your turn. Say: Suppose.

35
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:52.772
Suppose.

36
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:54.808
Wish + would.

37
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:58.850
Wish + would means annoyance about someone's behaviour.

38
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.869
I wish he would stop.

39
00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:04.519
Your turn. Say: Wish + would.

40
00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.751
Wish + would.

41
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:10.738
Hypothetical.

42
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.970
Hypothetical means imagined, not real.

43
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.304
A hypothetical case.

44
00:02:16.917 --> 00:02:19.499
Your turn. Say: Hypothetical.

45
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:23.300
Hypothetical.

46
00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.809
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.786
Visal, what is the difference between I'd rather you stayed and I'd rather stay?

48
00:02:33.883 --> 00:02:44.674
When the subject is the same, I'd rather stay uses the bare infinitive. When the subjects differ, use the past: I'd rather you stayed, which is an unreal present preference.

49
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:47.353
What about it's about time?

50
00:02:48.450 --> 00:03:00.588
It's about time we left uses the past simple, even though we mean now. Both it's time and it's high time work this way, and they express that something should have happened already.

51
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:03.068
And wishes with would?

52
00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:20.004
I wish you would listen expresses annoyance about behaviour. If only is stronger: If only he would listen. Supposing and suppose introduce hypothetical situations: Suppose you had a choice, what would you do?

53
00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.737
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:31.458
Grammar focus: Preferences: would rather plus base (same subject) and plus past (different subject); it's time plus past.

55
00:03:31.758 --> 00:03:32.921
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:35.477
I would rather you stayed at home.

57
00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:37.884
It's about time we left.

58
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:40.202
I wish he would listen.

59
00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:50.012
Would rather + different subject takes the past. It's about time + past. Wish + would shows annoyance. If only is stronger than wish.

60
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.878
Be careful! Don't say: I'd rather you to go.

61
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:57.473
Say: I'd rather you went.

62
00:03:57.773 --> 00:03:59.645
Use the past after rather.

63
00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:03.179
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:03.967 --> 00:04:05.374
I'd Rather, If Only.

65
00:04:05.674 --> 00:04:08.568
I would rather you did not tell anyone about the surprise.

66
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:12.170
It's about time the council repaired the road.

67
00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.619
I wish the neighbours would turn the music down.

68
00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:19.097
If only the weather were warmer, we could swim.

69
00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.622
Supposing you had a choice, which would you take?

70
00:04:23.733 --> 00:04:27.967
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:28.817 --> 00:04:30.596
I'd rather you blank here.

72
00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:35.130
A, stay. B, stayed. C, will stay.

73
00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.550
The answer is B: stayed.

74
00:04:41.717 --> 00:04:43.310
It's about time we blank.

75
00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.718
A, left. B, leave. C, will leave.

76
00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.231
The answer is A: left.

77
00:04:53.383 --> 00:04:55.244
I wish he blank stop talking.

78
00:04:55.544 --> 00:04:58.466
A, would. B, will. C, is.

79
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.465
The answer is A: would.

80
00:05:04.617 --> 00:05:05.815
Which is correct?

81
00:05:06.115 --> 00:05:10.593
A, I'd rather you to go.. B, I'd rather you went.. C, I'd rather you go..

82
00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:16.679
The answer is B: I'd rather you went..

83
00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:21.082
According to the reading, what should the council repair?

84
00:05:21.382 --> 00:05:25.151
A, the road. B, the school. C, the bridge.

85
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.583
The answer is A: the road.

86
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.940
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:40.082
Write two sentences expressing a preference using 'would rather' and 'it's about time'.

88
00:05:48.883 --> 00:05:50.279
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.579 --> 00:06:01.767
I would rather you told me the truth than lied. It's about time we started the project. Both sentences use a past form to talk about the present, which marks an unreal situation.

90
00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:03.603
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:04.517 --> 00:06:13.380
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and preferences: would rather plus base (same subject) and plus past (different subject); it's time plus past.

92
00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.726
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:18.026 --> 00:06:20.748
See you in Unit thirty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:06:21.048 --> 00:06:23.967
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

